cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "frapscope: fluorescence recovery after photobleaching for live-cell imaging"
abstract: >-
  Extraction of FRAP recovery series directly from Leica .lif archives, double
  normalisation against an unbleached reference, point-based mobile-fraction
  estimation from a measured plateau, and comparison of conditions under a
  contrast family fixed by experimental design. Replicates recovering above
  their own pre-bleach level are excluded as physically impossible rather than
  clamped, and the smallest p-value the exact rank null can return at the given
  replicate counts is reported alongside the observed one.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-11"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sukhanovaxenia/frapscope"
authors:
  - family-names: Sukhanova
    given-names: Xenia
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7022-0832"
    affiliation: "Laboratory of Amyloid Biology, Saint Petersburg State University"
keywords:
  - FRAP
  - fluorescence recovery after photobleaching
  - live-cell imaging
  - biomolecular condensates
  - protein aggregation
  - bioimage analysis
